      "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $42$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{5}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=42$ and $r=-\\frac{1}{5}.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{42[1-{(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{N}]}{1-(-\\frac{1}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{42[1-{(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{N}]}{\\frac{6}{5}} \\\\  & =35[1-{(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{N}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
